local-patch (2026-06-05) — NOT verbatim upstream:
  WHAT:  the bundled proc.sh probes the parent process with `ps -f | awk '{... printf $i" " ...}'`,
         using the process-argv field as a printf FORMAT string. Changed both probes to
         `printf "%s ", $i`.
  WHERE: executable_batpipe lines 123 and 149 (proc.sh: parent_executable / parent_shell).
  WHY:   batpipe walks its whole process-ancestor tree to detect whether it runs inside less/bat.
         With the field-as-format bug, gawk aborts ("fatal: not enough arguments to satisfy
         format string") whenever ANY ancestor's argv contains a % conversion (e.g. a wrapping
         `sh -c '...%s...'`). That crashed parent-detection, so `less <file>` fell back to the raw
         file — no syntax highlighting, raw archive bytes. Reproduced on AlmaLinux 9 / gawk 5.1.0.
  UPSTREAM: still present in master (lib/proc.sh:14,60) as of release v2024.08.24. Not yet reported
         upstream — re-apply this patch on every bump until upstream fixes it.

files:          executable_batpipe  (prebuilt standalone bin/batpipe from the release zip; bat-modules bundled inline; + local-patch above)
note:           Leading-dot filename → chezmoi-ignored; provenance only, never deployed.
                Deploys 0755 to ~/.local/bin/batpipe (executable_ prefix); wired as the less LESSOPEN
                preprocessor via `eval "$(batpipe)"` in dot_zshrc.tmpl + dot_bashrc.tmpl.
                No versions.mk entry — pinned only here (not coupled to BAT_VERSION).
                Bump: re-download the release zip, replace executable_batpipe with bin/batpipe,
                RE-APPLY the local-patch above, then refresh release + asset-sha256 + both file-sha256 here.
